  "verificationNotes": [
    "Initial commerce and multi-currency evidence uses an isolated database clone and a Git archive of the exact selected RC3 source. The actual development service now uses published RC3 gems and an application-owned Store API price-ordering provider.",
    "Both RC3 engine migrations and the upgrade tasks completed. Commerce preflight verified no pending migrations, required ownership columns, decimal(19,4) money columns, and the store-scoped Stripe test gateway. A pre-migration negative probe failed as expected.",
    "The read-only browser suite reached the isolated RC3 backend with the Cloudflare process-environment override enabled. Earlier runs against the existing RC1 service are excluded.",
    "Actual responses carry decimal-string product and facet amounts and Market country_codes. KWD four-decimal unit prices, JPY zero-decimal prices, and regional locales were checked in rendered pages.",
    "SDK commerce probes verified delivery cost and selected rate retention, full Store Credit single-order completion, full Gift Card multi-seller completion, completed-Cart and group lookup, child Channel ownership, and unrelated-guest denial. These probes do not certify browser cookies or UI recovery.",
    "Guest test-card, saved-card, discount, delivery, billing-address, cart-reload, and normal OrderGroup browser scenarios passed locally. The latest complete checkout run passed 17 of 19 scenarios; two stopped at Stripe field initialization. A targeted retry passed required-field validation but still failed to initialize card fields for lost-response OrderGroup recovery. The complete suite remains unpassed.",
    "Full Gift Card OrderGroup and Store Credit single-order browser completion, confirmation reload, and unrelated-guest denial passed on an isolated published-gem backend. Store Credit was applied through the configured backend service to the browser-owned test cart, not through a storefront balance-application UI. The observed zero-due payment-reset render loop was fixed and reverified with no console errors. Lost-response OrderGroup recovery and wallet callbacks remain open.",
    "A focused Stripe browser retry passed all three scenarios without test retries, payment-code changes, or increased waits: saved-card to new-card switching, guest test-card completion with confirmation reload, and provider decline followed by successful retry. All six Elements session requests returned HTTP 200 in 730-2181 ms. This is consistent with a transient network or service issue, but does not prove the earlier root cause or replace the complete checkout suite.",
    "Jobs were held and mail delivery disabled in the isolated backend. Deployed staging, rollback, jobs, mail, storage, webhooks, shared cache, backups, and live payments are not verified.",
    "The built-in RC3 price sorter still aggregates unrelated currency and price-list rows. The development application now replaces Store API database price ordering with serializer-equivalent price resolution before pagination; both directions and empty results pass locally. Deployed Market-aware shared-cache behavior remains open.",
    "The initial read-only audit compared the then-RC1 development service with the isolated RC3 source backend and reproduced price-ordering mismatches. The development service has since been upgraded to published RC3 gems and the application-owned ordering fix has passed backend, Store API, and browser checks. The frontend application gate passes with the separately modified dependency worktree; those dependency files are not included in these follow-up commits.",
    "The actual development seller now has its own delivery method copied from an existing USD 5 rate and zone. Platform methods remain unshared; owner, operator, and other-seller scope checks passed without persisting a verification purchase. The complete browser suite used an isolated shared-method fixture; subsequent full-balance browser probes used the seller-owned policy."
  ]
